mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course takes the Human Body Science Museum as its physical base, telling students the history behind the slices, revisiting the touching stories of the museum's pioneers, and leading them on a journey through the fascinating microscopic world.</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Through this course, students will be able to:</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Gain an in-depth understanding of the historical stories of microtomes and microscopes;</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Experience the charm of modern giant microtomes;</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Explore the fascinating microscopic world on the virtual microscopy experiment platform;</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Listen to the humanistic stories behind the specimens;</span><br><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Discover the art of the human body through medical paintings.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
